hey are really enjoying  the opportunity they're not likely to  leave unless you give them a reason to  leave so you want to give them trust you  want to show them they have  opportunities to develop and that you  know it's a fun place to work they're  going to learn a lot there's  opportunities for growth they have a  chance to do what they're excited and  passionate about and you want to be a  supportive boss as much as you can so  they don't have it a reason to want to  leave right if people come to work every  day they're really happy  doing it they're not going to want to  leave or if they're thinking about  starting their own business it's going  to be a lot harder to want to do compare  it to you they had a really bad box who  treated them like garbage and you know  they didn't you know get along with them  very well they didn't enjoy the work  environment so treat them well you know  have a good place where people want to  work and they won't have a strong  incentive to want to leave you and go  somewhere else so the first part is  build that system so it's not just a  sales person they see that leaving they  would be missing everybody else in the  business that kind of makes it run and  then to make it a good place to work  where people don't want to leave you now  it doesn't mean they're not going to  leave you you can never completely avoid  that but that will help prevent it as  much as possible and hopefully give you  employees who want to stay with you for  a very long time so hopefully that helps  Chris if you guys like the video please  give it a thumbs up below and I'd also  love to hear you have to think you can  run leave a comment under the video or  if you have something else to add to  chris's question then please leave it  below and we'll see you on the next  episode  you  you
 

